description:
The final project reads commands like `add 2026-03-01 -12.50 food "Lunch with Ada" --tag=work --split`. Write the parser:

```csharp
public record ParsedCommand(
    string Name,
    IReadOnlyList<string> Args,
    IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string> Options,
    IReadOnlySet<string> Flags);

public static class CommandParser
{
    public static List<string> Tokenize(string line)
    public static ParsedCommand? Parse(string line)
}
```

**Tokenize** splits on spaces (runs of spaces count as one). A token can be quoted with `"`; inside quotes spaces are kept and `\"` is a quote and `\\` a backslash. Quotes may start in the middle of a token: `a"b c"d` is one token `ab cd`. An unclosed quote throws `FormatException("unclosed quote")`. `""` is an empty token.

**Parse** tokenizes, then:
- returns `null` for a blank line;
- the first token, in lower case, is the `Name`;
- `--key=value` sets an option (keys in lower case; the value keeps its case and may be empty); a later one with the same key wins;
- `--flag` (no `=`) adds a flag in lower case;
- a token `--` on its own ends the options: every token after it is an argument, even if it starts with `--`;
- everything else is an argument, in order. Only unquoted tokens can be options or flags: `"--x"` in quotes is an argument.

